## Phase 3A – Assurance Explanation Engine

### Purpose

Convert deterministic assurance outcomes into human-readable explanations.

The Assurance Engine determines assurance status.

The Assurance Explanation Engine explains assurance status.

### Architecture

Requirement
↓
Policy Agent
↓
Suggested Claims
↓
Dashboard Approval
↓
Approved Claims
↓
Evidence Collection
↓
Claim Assurance
↓
Requirement Assurance
↓
Assurance Explanation Engine
↓
Dashboard

### Responsibilities

Requirement Assurance Engine

* Evaluate claim results
* Determine requirement status

Assurance Explanation Engine

* Explain requirement outcomes
* Explain evidence gaps
* Explain failed claims
* Generate recommendations

### Governance Principle

The explanation engine does not influence assurance outcomes.

Assurance remains evidence-based and deterministic.

The explanation engine only interprets results already produced by the assurance system.

### Example

Requirement Status

PARTIALLY_ASSURED

Supporting Evidence

* Service exists

Missing Evidence

* response_time
* failure_rate

Generated Explanation

The requirement is partially assured.

The service exists and has been observed in runtime reality.

However, service health cannot currently be justified because response time and failure rate evidence are unavailable.

Recommended next step:

Enable collection of response time and failure rate evidence.

### Future Evolution

Current

Deterministic explanation generation.

Future

Gemini-powered explanation generation.

The explanation contract remains unchanged.
